1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Northern Finland.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:07,500
Veikko has just replaced an optical module on node TRN-042.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,000
The link is up, optics are normal, alarms have cleared,

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
but traffic isn't coming back.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
He asks Erkki, a senior network expert.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Erkki has seen this before.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Twelve messages.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
One sentence of real knowledge.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,500
And it was never written down.

10
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:33,000
Hidden knowledge?

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Not anymore.

12
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,000
This is ElidEx.

13
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,500
ElidEx listens to the chats and emails people already use.

14
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,000
No form, no tag, no extra click.

15
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
It finds the few sentences that matter and turns them into a rule an agent can read.

16
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,500
Then it links that rule to the right place in the network: TRN-042,

17
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,500
and the older units like it.

18
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:02,500
Not every node. A wrong link is worse than none.

19
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:08,000
And every rule keeps its source and how far to trust it.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
4:00 AM.

21
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Same symptom on TRN-088, another older unit.

22
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,000
Erkki is asleep, and nobody needs to wake him.

23
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,500
The agent asks ElidEx and gets his fix, with its source.

24
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,000
The technician reports back: traffic's back, and the rule gets stronger.

25
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
And the day never ends.

26
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
New chats every few minutes. Most of them noise.

27
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:35,000
It also learns directly from the network itself.

28
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,500
Three different faults, all hanging off one node that nobody mentioned.

29
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,500
That's where the team should look first.

30
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:46,500
And it spots the same problem coming back on different units.

31
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,500
Erkki's trick was needed on three of them,

32
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:54,000
and the lasting fix—firmware 4.2—hasn't reached them yet.

33
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,500
So the company can fix it once and for all.

34
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:01,000
The knowledge was always there, hidden in everyday conversations.

35
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Knowledge is precious.

36
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
ElidEx makes sure it's never lost.

37
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Tomorrow at 8:00, the agents will know a little more.

38
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
And Erkki might finally get a quiet morning.
